00:18:45.791 --> 00:18:47.759
So these guys fly in on a private jet


00:18:47.835 --> 00:18:51.339
and their idea of fun is rubbing
a burnt cork on each ether's faces?


00:18:51.422 --> 00:18:53.049
That's insane.


00:18:53.132 --> 00:18:57.012
Sanity's overrated.
Tried it once, didn't get it.


00:18:59.805 --> 00:19:01.478
Join in. We don't bite.


00:19:01.557 --> 00:19:05.232
Well, my mum bites a bit. The rest of us
just nibble ibble dibble...


00:19:05.311 --> 00:19:06.813
Talking crap.


00:19:06.896 --> 00:19:09.445
- You! it's time.
- No, there's absolutely no way.


00:19:09.523 --> 00:19:11.867
- Yes! Yes!
-I don't want to!


00:19:13.819 --> 00:19:16.789
Georgie! Georgie! Georgie! Georgie!


00:19:16.864 --> 00:19:18.958
OK, OK.


00:19:19.033 --> 00:19:20.501
Hark! The Herald.


00:19:23.913 --> 00:19:24.960
Ooh.


00:19:25.039 --> 00:19:29.419
(makes farting sounds to tune of
"Hark! The Herald Angels Sing'Q


00:19:34.465 --> 00:19:37.014
(mimics beatbox)


00:19:37.093 --> 00:19:39.846
- Go, go, go.
- (Chloe) Oh, Nigel.


00:19:39.929 --> 00:19:41.306
(Dickie) Yeah, yeah, yeah.


00:19:44.642 --> 00:19:48.021
See now, this is my idea of fun.
You should join in.


00:19:48.104 --> 00:19:51.028
(all) J' Hark! The herald angels sing


00:19:51.107 --> 00:19:55.112
Unfortunately I'm only grade one
at... whatever that is.


00:19:57.363 --> 00:19:59.081
Yeah!


00:19:59.156 --> 00:20:02.877
- You eating alright?
- Five a day. How's it going?


00:20:02.952 --> 00:20:05.626
- It's fine.
- What are the people like?


00:20:05.705 --> 00:20:07.707
- (excited shrieking)
- They're...


00:20:07.790 --> 00:20:09.667
Who wants more champagne?


00:20:09.750 --> 00:20:11.423
..fine.


00:20:11.502 --> 00:20:14.881
If it doesn't work out, I can
always nick one of their paintings.


00:20:14.964 --> 00:20:17.012
- (beeping)
- What's that noise?


00:20:17.091 --> 00:20:19.514
Oh, nothing, er...


00:20:19.593 --> 00:20:23.518
No, it's next door.
There's a truck reversing,


00:20:23.597 --> 00:20:25.224
I think.


00:20:27.017 --> 00:20:29.270
Listen, Kimmy,


00:20:29.353 --> 00:20:30.946
I really miss you, you know?


00:20:31.021 --> 00:20:34.400
I know, Dad. Me too.


00:20:41.574 --> 00:20:44.703
(Kim) Georgie? Georgie?


00:20:45.786 --> 00:20:47.379
It's seven.


00:20:47.455 --> 00:20:49.503
(Georgie groans)


00:20:51.083 --> 00:20:52.460
Rule two?


00:20:59.925 --> 00:21:02.553
- Is this caviar?
- Sure looks like it.


00:21:02.636 --> 00:21:07.688
Well, dig in, everyone,
and enjoy your $300 omelettes.


00:21:09.477 --> 00:21:14.859
Jesus, Kim. You have to wake me.
I don't need you making me look bad.


00:21:14.940 --> 00:21:17.363
- No kidding.
- (shrieks)


00:21:17.443 --> 00:21:20.117
So what am I supposed
to do all day, then?


00:21:20.196 --> 00:21:25.669
I don't know. I'm sure
you'll find something. Look around.


00:21:54.814 --> 00:21:56.111
Oh, shit.


00:21:57.191 --> 00:21:59.285
Wait! Stop!


00:22:17.044 --> 00:22:19.672
- Georgie, this cake is supreme.
- Thank you, Jonny.


00:22:19.755 --> 00:22:21.757
(Nigel) Hm-hmm! Sure is.


00:22:21.882 --> 00:22:24.806
- This place is so magical.
- It is when you're here.


00:22:24.969 --> 00:22:28.143
Enjoy it. You won't ski this much
when you're starting a family.


00:22:28.222 --> 00:22:31.476
- Do I get a say in any of this?
- No, snoogles, you don't.


00:22:31.559 --> 00:22:35.189
I'm not sure I'm ready for any of this.
Do I look like a grandfather?


00:22:35.271 --> 00:22:37.649
- Don't answer that!
- (Chloe laughs)


00:22:39.066 --> 00:22:41.615
Thank you. Ooh.


00:22:42.736 --> 00:22:44.659
(shrieks)


00:22:44.738 --> 00:22:46.285
That's hot!


00:23:02.047 --> 00:23:07.144
I Angels watching over me
with smiles upon their face


00:23:07.219 --> 00:23:12.396
J' Cos I have made it through this far
in an unforgiving place


00:23:12.474 --> 00:23:17.196
J' it feels sometimes this hill's
too steep for a girl like me to climb


00:23:18.314 --> 00:23:20.942
I But I must knock those thoughts
right down


00:23:21.025 --> 00:23:23.073
I I'll do it in my own time


00:23:23.152 --> 00:23:24.950
J* I don't care


00:23:25.029 --> 00:23:27.498
I I?n halfway there


00:23:28.616 --> 00:23:32.041
J* On a road that leads me
straight to who knows where


00:23:32.202 --> 00:23:33.374
(yells)


00:23:38.125 --> 00:23:40.719
You crazy freak!
Watch where you're going!


00:23:40.794 --> 00:23:42.592
I'm so sorry. Sorry.


00:23:42.671 --> 00:23:45.641
Stay safe, Betty Boop.
Hang outside on the ripside!


00:23:45.716 --> 00:23:50.438
- Yeah, and in English?
- Hang outside on the ripside.


00:23:52.848 --> 00:23:54.100
Ciao!


00:23:54.183 --> 00:23:56.436
.P I tell you what


00:23:56.518 --> 00:23:59.317
I What I have found


00:23:59.396 --> 00:24:02.070
I That I?n no fool


00:24:02.149 --> 00:24:04.868
J* I'm just upside down


00:24:04.944 --> 00:24:07.117
I Ain 't got no cares


00:24:07.196 --> 00:24:10.291
I I ain 't got no rules


00:24:10.366 --> 00:24:12.869
J' I think I like


00:24:12.952 --> 00:24:15.705
I Living upside down


00:24:18.374 --> 00:24:19.796
I You gotta slow it down


00:24:19.875 --> 00:24:22.424
- (yells)
- J' But then you pick it up


00:24:23.504 --> 00:24:26.974
J' Come on and try a little topsy-tun/y
back-to-front the right way round


00:24:29.969 --> 00:24:32.597
You blow at boarding.
But you sure are styley.


00:24:32.680 --> 00:24:35.274
I'll take it you're not
into pink all-in-ones?


00:24:35.349 --> 00:24:36.566
(laughs)


00:24:40.187 --> 00:24:45.739
- Mikki. Single guy from Finland.
- Kim. Not interested from England.


00:24:47.069 --> 00:24:49.868
- You know the skateboarding?
- A bit.


00:24:49.989 --> 00:24:52.458
Same, same, but different.
You want some help?


00:24:54.660 --> 00:24:57.334
- Yeah.
- OK, come on, get up.


00:25:00.165 --> 00:25:04.841
OK, in skateboarding, weight back.
In snowboarding, weight centred.


00:25:04.962 --> 00:25:08.512
OK. Right.


00:25:08.590 --> 00:25:10.308
- Knees.
- OK.


00:25:13.220 --> 00:25:15.973
Turn with your shoulders,
not the knees.


00:25:16.974 --> 00:25:19.068
You're a natural.


00:25:19.143 --> 00:25:20.941
It's like skateboarding, huh?


00:25:21.061 --> 00:25:22.404
(Kim) Whoo-hoo!


00:25:22.479 --> 00:25:23.901
(laughs)


00:25:25.357 --> 00:25:28.201
- That was pretty cool.
- That was nothing, Betty.


00:25:28.277 --> 00:25:30.120
Let's get high.


00:25:30.195 --> 00:25:31.788
UP-


00:25:31.864 --> 00:25:35.118
Oh. No, I can't. I'm on the budget tour.


00:25:35.200 --> 00:25:37.828
Betty... Follow me.


00:25:48.922 --> 00:25:52.517
Hey, look. That's the biggest
snowboarding competition in Tyrol.


00:25:52.593 --> 00:25:56.439
Every year I enter,
every year I face-plant.


00:25:56.513 --> 00:25:58.686
But this year I rock it!


00:25:58.766 --> 00:26:01.064
Hey, we'll enter together.


00:26:01.143 --> 00:26:03.441
Why? Because I'm such a pro boarder?


00:26:03.520 --> 00:26:05.739
Three months, maybe.


00:26:05.814 --> 00:26:08.567
Maybe, maybe not.


00:26:08.650 --> 00:26:12.575
Come on. $25,000. it's easy for you.
You're a skateboarder.


00:26:12.654 --> 00:26:15.703
I pulled a 360 my first day on a board.


00:26:15.783 --> 00:26:19.003
- (Kim) And broke your neck, right?
- (Mikki) No. My leg.


00:26:20.454 --> 00:26:23.173
Just so you know,
I've given Jonny your mother's ring.


00:26:23.248 --> 00:26:27.094
That's a coincidence. I've given him
one of her dresses. He'll look lovely.


00:26:27.169 --> 00:26:29.922
It is not funny.
The marquee is pencilled for June.


00:26:30.005 --> 00:26:32.884
It was quite funny.


00:26:32.966 --> 00:26:36.311
Didn't you get the message?
You're joining us. Dress up.


00:26:37.221 --> 00:26:38.894
I... did.


00:26:38.972 --> 00:26:40.940
Don't worry. She made me change too.


00:26:41.016 --> 00:26:45.442
Drainpipe jeans and winkle-pickers
aren't very this season apparently.


00:26:47.439 --> 00:26:49.533
(Chloe) You were never a style guru.


00:26:49.608 --> 00:26:51.406
(Jonny) I was.


00:26:53.779 --> 00:26:55.998
Lippy.


00:26:56.115 --> 00:26:57.583
Liner.


00:26:57.658 --> 00:26:59.251
Lashes.


00:26:59.326 --> 00:27:01.328
Accessories.


00:27:01.411 --> 00:27:02.833
I want those back.


00:27:02.913 --> 00:27:06.087
And... hair gum. Use sparingly.


00:27:06.166 --> 00:27:07.964
Hair gum?


00:27:17.136 --> 00:27:18.809
And like that, she became a swan.


00:27:18.887 --> 00:27:20.889
So I used to be an ugly duckling, then?


00:27:20.973 --> 00:27:23.647
Someone needs to learn
how to take a compliment.


00:27:25.269 --> 00:27:28.864
- Ah, it all makes sense now.
- Yeah. I'm just back office.


00:27:34.653 --> 00:27:37.748
- It's a shoelace.
- Er, it's bow tie.


00:27:37.823 --> 00:27:41.327
No, it's a shoelace knot. Come here.


00:27:46.331 --> 00:27:49.756
Didn't think you'd be the kind of girl
who knew how to tie a bow tie.


00:27:49.835 --> 00:27:52.884
And here's me thinking
you were the kind of boy who would.


00:27:58.427 --> 00:28:00.805
Big night for you, then?


00:28:08.437 --> 00:28:10.781
There.


00:28:10.856 --> 00:28:12.950
Licensed to kill.


00:28:14.610 --> 00:28:17.363
- Or be killed.
- (laughs)


00:28:26.997 --> 00:28:29.466
(Jonny) Right, who needs a drink?


00:28:31.210 --> 00:28:36.137
- Oh, Georgie. What are these?
- Mini-burgers. Don't blame me.


00:28:36.256 --> 00:28:39.055
They are sensational.


00:28:39.134 --> 00:28:41.853
- Trying to get me drunk?
- Just helping you on your way.


00:28:41.929 --> 00:28:43.897
Greasing your nuts, as it were.


00:28:43.972 --> 00:28:46.851
- Rule three?
- Oh, shut up.


00:28:47.935 --> 00:28:49.983
What are you grinning at?


00:28:50.062 --> 00:28:53.316
Nothing. Just think
I'm starting to get the hang of this.


00:28:53.398 --> 00:28:57.403
The cake's on the oven. The beef
is nearly done. And the mousse has set.


00:28:57.486 --> 00:28:59.409
Oh, thank you.


00:29:01.740 --> 00:29:03.742
Thank you.


00:29:03.825 --> 00:29:06.624
- Wow. Did you hear what...
- Yeah, don't get used to it.


00:29:06.703 --> 00:29:08.705
Get a fresh one of these.


00:29:08.789 --> 00:29:11.417
Such responsibility.
Do I get a performance star?


00:29:11.500 --> 00:29:13.548
- What?
- Doesn't matter.


00:29:23.679 --> 00:29:25.727
Chloe, you look wonderful.


00:29:32.145 --> 00:29:36.821
Oh, look. Looks like the new girl's
putting on pre-dinner entertainment.


00:29:36.900 --> 00:29:39.449
Oh, dear, stand back.


00:29:39.528 --> 00:29:40.780
Kim, wait. Kim...


00:29:44.992 --> 00:29:47.461
(Caroline) What a waste. That's vintage.


00:29:53.625 --> 00:29:57.050
Doctor's orders. The good news is,
you've already got the headache,


00:29:57.129 --> 00:29:58.927
so you can drink as much as you like.


00:29:59.006 --> 00:30:01.509
- I should go and help Georgie.
- I wouldn't worry.


00:30:01.591 --> 00:30:04.686
- I think Nigel has her covered.
- Thanks.


00:30:09.641 --> 00:30:14.397
- Hit the spot.
- Yeah, it should. '62 Dom.


00:30:14.479 --> 00:30:17.824
- Dom?
- It's 500 quid a bottle.


00:30:17.899 --> 00:30:22.200
500? Think I'll just take the cash
next time.


00:30:24.406 --> 00:30:27.000
Why am I here?
I'm stuck in a parallel reality


00:30:27.075 --> 00:30:29.919
where people drink my monthly salary
every ten minutes.


00:30:29.995 --> 00:30:34.546
You're right. We're aliens.
My mother has a tail. Did you see it?


00:30:34.624 --> 00:30:36.922
Your mum is the scariest woman
I've ever met.


00:30:37.002 --> 00:30:40.381
You want to know how she met
my dad? Air stewardess. Concorde.


00:30:40.464 --> 00:30:43.308
Your dad was an air stewardess?


00:30:44.885 --> 00:30:46.228
She's not that scary.


00:30:49.056 --> 00:30:50.933
Well, look, I should be getting back.


00:30:51.016 --> 00:30:55.522
Yeah, of course. Thanks for the Dom.


00:30:57.898 --> 00:30:59.650
Yeah.


00:31:12.537 --> 00:31:14.460
(Jonny) Can we talk about this later?


00:31:14.539 --> 00:31:17.713
(Caroline)
She won't wait forever, Jonny.


00:31:17.793 --> 00:31:20.512
(sighs) I feel so sorry for her.


00:31:21.922 --> 00:31:23.515
See?


00:31:26.301 --> 00:31:28.178
- Thank you.
- Everything alright?


00:31:28.261 --> 00:31:31.982
Yeah, everything's fine.
We'll be back out in February.


00:31:32.057 --> 00:31:35.436
See if you can figure out the whole
champagne-bottle thing by then.


00:31:35.519 --> 00:31:39.240
- Yep, I will practise daily.
- Knock yourself out.


00:31:40.482 --> 00:31:43.577
Trying to shake your hand,
punch you in the stomach. Not cool.


00:31:43.652 --> 00:31:46.121
So, I'll put the photos on Facebook.


00:31:47.114 --> 00:31:49.367
Well,... poke me.


00:31:51.034 --> 00:31:53.457
Right. OK, girls.


00:31:53.537 --> 00:31:57.041
This is for all your hard work.
Thank you so much.


00:31:57.124 --> 00:32:00.128
And, Kim, you know you get
a lift pass too, don't you?


00:32:00.210 --> 00:32:04.807
Just charge it to the chalet.
Unless you'd prefer the cash.


00:32:04.881 --> 00:32:07.134
- Lift pass would be great.
- OK.


00:32:07.217 --> 00:32:10.187
- Alright, let's go.
- It's a private plane. It can wait.


00:32:10.262 --> 00:32:13.015
- It will. I won't.
- Desperate to get back to work.


00:32:13.098 --> 00:32:15.942
OK, maybe I'll quit,
and next time we can hitchhike here.


00:32:16.017 --> 00:32:18.896
A father-son adventure.
I like the sound of that. Bye.


00:32:24.776 --> 00:32:27.404
- "Poke me"?
- Piss off.


00:32:27.529 --> 00:32:29.076
Slut.


00:32:30.532 --> 00:32:33.160
- 200-euro tip for one week?
- (microwave pings)


00:32:33.243 --> 00:32:35.086
Are you sure you're just cooking?


00:32:35.162 --> 00:32:39.042
I'll put it in the bank when I can.
You OK?


00:32:39.833 --> 00:32:41.676
- Yeah. Solid.
- Huh?


00:32:41.751 --> 00:32:43.674
I mean sound, yeah.


00:32:43.753 --> 00:32:47.383
- Don't let them work you too hard.
- I won't.


00:32:59.352 --> 00:33:02.196
(Kim) Right, Finland, let's do this.
Where do we start?


00:33:02.272 --> 00:33:07.403
Well, in slopestyle, you are scored
on your tricks on the rails,


00:33:07.486 --> 00:33:09.204
and the jump you pull at the end.


00:33:09.279 --> 00:33:13.125
- You smell me?
- Yes, I smell you. Unfortunately.


00:33:14.701 --> 00:33:18.672
Think about the run. Only the run.
Be the board.


00:33:22.000 --> 00:33:24.253
Let's get tricky with Mikki!


00:33:24.336 --> 00:33:26.054
(yells)


00:33:28.507 --> 00:33:29.633
(whoops)


00:33:30.800 --> 00:33:32.928
Right, come on, Kim.


00:33:37.766 --> 00:33:39.359
(yells)


00:33:48.235 --> 00:33:49.828
(whoops)


00:33:52.572 --> 00:33:54.666
Yes! (whoops)


00:33:59.454 --> 00:34:02.003
- Hey.
- Hey.


00:34:02.082 --> 00:34:06.337
You do realise you're riding a beginner
board from, like, the 16th century?


00:34:06.419 --> 00:34:09.923
I thought the 16th century
was the golden age of snowboarding.


00:34:10.006 --> 00:34:12.885
Go to the rental shop
and pick yourself up a park board.


00:34:12.968 --> 00:34:15.141
You'll have more fun on that, trust me.


00:34:15.220 --> 00:34:19.396
And ask for Willy. Tell him
Tara sent you. He'll hook you up.


00:34:20.517 --> 00:34:22.815
Stay safe out there.


00:34:23.436 --> 00:34:24.904
Thanks.


00:34:36.741 --> 00:34:37.993
Kann ich dir helfen?


00:34:39.369 --> 00:34:41.747
Oh, I'm just looking, thanks.


00:34:41.830 --> 00:34:46.051
Rentals are only 80 euros a week,
and half-price for staff.


00:34:46.751 --> 00:34:51.006
Well, I'm staff. And actually,
Tara told me to come by.


00:34:51.089 --> 00:34:53.933
OK, fine. 30.


00:34:54.009 --> 00:34:57.934
Freestyle board, boots and helmet.
You get top end for that.


00:35:09.316 --> 00:35:11.410
Cool. Deal.


00:35:13.278 --> 00:35:16.999
J* For such a long time


00:35:17.073 --> 00:35:20.623
J* We've been standing in line


00:35:20.702 --> 00:35:24.377
.P And it's been so long


00:35:24.456 --> 00:35:28.962
Whoo!


00:35:33.923 --> 00:35:35.596
- Georgie!
- Hey!


00:35:37.177 --> 00:35:39.100
Check it out! That's your buddy, Kim.


00:35:39.179 --> 00:35:40.601
Whoo!


00:35:41.765 --> 00:35:44.735
I thought you said she hadn't been
in the mountains before.


00:35:44.851 --> 00:35:46.478
She hadn't.


00:35:46.561 --> 00:35:47.608
I Far away with me


00:35:47.687 --> 00:35:49.689
J* You will never know


00:35:49.814 --> 00:35:52.693
(Dad) Hey, Kimmy.
I've got my first interview tomorrow.


00:35:52.817 --> 00:35:57.448
And, well, I'm being a good boy and
going through the statements, but I saw


00:35:57.530 --> 00:36:00.249
that tip money hasn't gone in.
it's probably their fault


00:36:00.325 --> 00:36:02.123
but I just thought I'd let you know.


00:36:02.202 --> 00:36:07.459
And, hey, Kimmy, aubergines. Whoo!
My new favourite food. Who knew?


00:36:07.540 --> 00:36:09.008
Alright, Kimmy, love you.


00:36:15.674 --> 00:36:17.301
(alarm clock beeps)


00:36:24.974 --> 00:36:27.602
- Didn't hear you get up.
- I haven't.


00:36:56.506 --> 00:36:59.430
Level nine! Yeah, baby.


00:37:03.388 --> 00:37:05.686
You really think
you're going to win that pro?


00:37:05.765 --> 00:37:07.312
N-N-No.


00:37:07.392 --> 00:37:09.394
(Bernhardt) Hallo!


00:37:09.477 --> 00:37:12.481
Abend. Friulein.


00:37:12.564 --> 00:37:15.818
- Hey, Bernie.
- What's with the towel, Bernie?


00:37:15.942 --> 00:37:20.072
My name is Bernhardt. Mr Madsen,
he asked me to test the hot tub.


00:37:20.155 --> 00:37:22.408
- Did he now?
- Jawohl.


00:37:23.324 --> 00:37:27.955
There is, you must know,
room for more than just one.


00:37:28.079 --> 00:37:30.753
That is so funny,


00:37:30.832 --> 00:37:33.130
because Kim and I were just saying


00:37:33.209 --> 00:37:35.928
how much we would love
to share a hot tub with Bernhardt.


00:37:36.004 --> 00:37:39.554
- For sure?
- Yeah.


00:37:39.632 --> 00:37:43.102
But the problem is,
we don't have our swimsuits.


00:37:43.178 --> 00:37:45.226
Who needs swimsuits?


