Strudel, nudel and... kniidel.


00:57:53.971 --> 00:57:58.351
I wouldn't mind a "canoodle"
with this one in fact.


00:57:58.475 --> 00:58:01.729
Right, nearest the pin, lads.
it's 50s in and it's...


00:58:01.812 --> 00:58:03.689
I'm going to go 32C.


00:58:03.772 --> 00:58:06.616
It's hard to tell. The jumper
might be bulking her up.


00:58:06.692 --> 00:58:08.615
Put me down for a 30B.


00:58:08.694 --> 00:58:11.868
Miles off. I'm thinking 30D,
the Holy Grail of bra sizes.


00:58:11.947 --> 00:58:14.996
Controversial. Go on, Kimmy,
put us out of our misery.


00:58:15.075 --> 00:58:16.952
No, Kim, don't answer that.


00:58:18.120 --> 00:58:21.750
I'm sorry. I was under the impression
that we were enjoying ourselves.


00:58:21.832 --> 00:58:25.587
Unlike most women you know, Malcolm,
Kim keeps her clothes on for a living.


00:58:25.669 --> 00:58:26.841
Oh.


00:58:26.920 --> 00:58:28.888
It's alright.
You know what they say.


00:58:28.964 --> 00:58:31.183
The bigger the chat,
the smaller the chap.


00:58:31.258 --> 00:58:33.681
(Dickie laughs)


00:58:33.760 --> 00:58:36.354
(Dickie) New game. Waistlines.
Malcolm?


00:58:39.599 --> 00:58:41.647
(Malcolm) Fantastic weekend, Dickie.


00:58:41.727 --> 00:58:44.071
Flattery will get you nowhere


00:58:44.146 --> 00:58:49.368
but some fresh powder and a couple of
tasty chalet tarts will get you 40 mill.


00:58:50.694 --> 00:58:53.948
- Dad, wait.
- Forgotten your hair-care products?


00:58:55.198 --> 00:58:58.998
Actually, I was thinking about staying
a couple more days if it's OK.


00:58:59.077 --> 00:59:03.708
Hey, do your thing.
Back for the weekend, obviously?


00:59:03.790 --> 00:59:05.713
Yeah, of course.


00:59:07.419 --> 00:59:09.262
I'll see you guys soon.


00:59:11.006 --> 00:59:14.886
There's, like, 400 euros here.
Should think so too. Bloody perverts.


00:59:14.968 --> 00:59:17.221
Jonny didn't ask us
to pay him back for...


00:59:17.304 --> 00:59:20.649
Thanks for reminding me.
(clears throat)


00:59:23.643 --> 00:59:28.240
- (Georgie laughs)
- Oh, and you. Yes.


00:59:30.275 --> 00:59:34.280
OK, so that you can earn yours back,
I want to hire you.


00:59:34.362 --> 00:59:36.330
50 euros an hour.


00:59:37.699 --> 00:59:40.122
Not like that.


00:59:42.704 --> 00:59:45.082
- Need a hand? The meter's running.
- No.


00:59:45.165 --> 00:59:48.089
That's three euros right there.
Well, it's your money.


00:59:48.168 --> 00:59:50.466
Actually, it's mine now. Again.


00:59:50.587 --> 00:59:53.716
Show me what's so great
about boarding. Let's get gnarled.


00:59:53.799 --> 00:59:56.552
- Gnarly.
- Whatever. Sick, phat, ill.


00:59:56.635 --> 00:59:58.353
You sound like a doctor.


01:00:01.139 --> 01:00:04.609
- Holy shit, I'm a natural.
- Shut up, snoogles.


01:00:08.396 --> 01:00:10.319
(Jonny) Move back into position.


01:00:10.398 --> 01:00:13.197
- (Jonny) Watch this one.
- (Kim) Now concentrate.


01:00:13.276 --> 01:00:15.654
- (Jonny) OK.
- Idiot.


01:00:15.737 --> 01:00:19.867
I think you mean, "Concentrate, please,
valued paying customer."


01:00:21.076 --> 01:00:24.501
- (Jonny) Oops.
- Owl


01:00:24.579 --> 01:00:29.631
- OK, that was an accident.
- I'm not going to be your bit of fun.


01:00:31.169 --> 01:00:35.049
- (Kim) Go on, then.
- Yes, yes, yes.


01:00:36.299 --> 01:00:38.722
(Kim) Come on, loser.
I'll show you how it's done.


01:00:47.686 --> 01:00:49.359
Yes!


01:00:49.437 --> 01:00:52.907
(Kim)
So you have a pretty rough life, huh?


01:00:52.983 --> 01:00:55.782
- (Jonny) Hideous, isn't it?
-I don't know how you stand it.


01:00:55.861 --> 01:00:57.613
It's not all it's cracked up to be.


01:00:57.696 --> 01:01:00.791
I've heard that having loads of money
can be a real let-down.


01:01:02.576 --> 01:01:05.125
You think I could do
anything I want to?


01:01:06.204 --> 01:01:10.835
Truth is, my dad's been saving a place
for me on the board since I was two


01:01:10.917 --> 01:01:13.636
and my mother won't be happy
until I've married Chloe


01:01:13.712 --> 01:01:16.716
and have nine children
with perfect teeth.


01:01:16.798 --> 01:01:18.675
They've got it all planned out for me


01:01:18.758 --> 01:01:21.762
and I'm, like,
"This is it? This is my life?"


01:01:24.639 --> 01:01:27.483
No, nice try, but not quite.


01:01:27.559 --> 01:01:30.483
Oh, angst. The rich kid's alternative
to real problems.


01:01:30.562 --> 01:01:34.863
Sarcasm. The chalet girl's alternative
to real humour. I know I'm lucky...


01:01:34.941 --> 01:01:37.069
"But I'm stuck in this caged existence


01:01:37.152 --> 01:01:39.496
of vintage champagne
and luxury ski chalets


01:01:39.571 --> 01:01:41.699
when I just want to be a pop star."


01:01:41.781 --> 01:01:43.954
Rock star.


01:01:50.457 --> 01:01:53.882
- Why don't you just do it, then?
- it's just not that simple.


01:01:56.546 --> 01:01:59.470
- What?
- it's nothing.


01:01:59.549 --> 01:02:02.143
No, what? Go on.


01:02:02.219 --> 01:02:04.597
It's just a bit silly.
My mum always used to say,


01:02:04.721 --> 01:02:08.146
"You've got brains in your head,
feet in your shoes."


01:02:08.225 --> 01:02:11.274
"You can steer yourself
in any direction you choose."


01:02:14.397 --> 01:02:15.819
Clever girl, your mum.


01:02:21.529 --> 01:02:23.623
Yeah. We should get going.


01:02:24.866 --> 01:02:26.243
(Jonny) Yeah.


01:02:27.702 --> 01:02:29.921
(Georgie)
I hope you know what you're doing.


01:02:31.539 --> 01:02:33.086
- Excuse me?
- I'm just saying.


01:02:33.166 --> 01:02:37.296
The season ends, he goes back
to his world, you go back to yours.


01:02:37.379 --> 01:02:38.676
What are you left with?


01:02:38.755 --> 01:02:42.726
(scoffs) My world?
Where exactly is that? Pluto?


01:02:42.801 --> 01:02:46.180
- No, that's not what I meant.
- Don't judge me by your standards.


01:02:46.263 --> 01:02:48.357
You'd rather be with a rich idiot
like Nigel


01:02:48.431 --> 01:02:51.401
instead of Mikki
who you are clearly in love with.


01:02:51.476 --> 01:02:55.276
- I'm going for a beer.
- There's something you need to know.


01:02:55.355 --> 01:02:59.235
I think I'm done
on the friendly advice for now, thanks.


01:02:59.317 --> 01:03:02.821
It'd be better
if you just stay out of it, OK?


01:03:06.616 --> 01:03:09.870
Do you want to talk about it?
A barman's cheaper than a shrink.


01:03:10.829 --> 01:03:12.923
A beer's cheaper than a barman.


01:03:13.748 --> 01:03:17.753
- I'm pretty cheap.
- Beer doesn't talk back either.


01:03:40.859 --> 01:03:42.827
(Jonny) Hey. Are you OK?


01:03:42.902 --> 01:03:47.157
- She told you where I was, then?
- I'm staying out of it.


01:03:47.866 --> 01:03:49.868
Look, about us...


01:03:51.494 --> 01:03:52.916
Night, Jonny.


01:03:54.664 --> 01:03:58.259
What I really came to say was
I booked the helicopter again.


01:04:00.045 --> 01:04:02.389
I need someone to serve me lunch.


01:04:04.299 --> 01:04:06.176
You are so annoying.


01:04:19.522 --> 01:04:20.944
I I feel sweet


01:04:21.024 --> 01:04:23.493
J' Do you feel sweet?


01:04:23.568 --> 01:04:25.320
.P It's amazing


01:04:29.157 --> 01:04:33.333
J' I have no skin,
and I feel everything


01:04:33.411 --> 01:04:35.084
.P It's amazing


01:04:39.084 --> 01:04:41.382
I I've wanted this for so long


01:04:41.461 --> 01:04:43.964
I Now the deed has been done


01:04:44.047 --> 01:04:46.971
I We shall rise with the sun


01:04:47.050 --> 01:04:49.394
J' Spend our time as one


01:04:58.603 --> 01:05:02.653
I Now there is no sin in anything


01:05:02.732 --> 01:05:04.530
.P it's life-changing


01:05:05.652 --> 01:05:08.246
J' This feeling


01:05:19.416 --> 01:05:21.134
J' This feeling


01:05:26.548 --> 01:05:28.642
J' This feeling


01:05:31.428 --> 01:05:33.351
.P It's amazing


01:05:37.434 --> 01:05:39.152
J* From now on


01:05:40.061 --> 01:05:42.484
J* From now on


01:05:42.564 --> 01:05:45.067
J* We are one


01:05:45.150 --> 01:05:47.323
.P It's amazing


01:05:47.402 --> 01:05:50.281
J* it's in the stars, in the sun


01:05:50.363 --> 01:05:52.411
.P it's everywhere, in everyone


01:05:52.490 --> 01:05:56.211
I And it will be every day


01:05:57.162 --> 01:06:01.838
J* From now on


01:06:01.958 --> 01:06:03.801
J* We are one


01:06:04.627 --> 01:06:07.471
.P It's amazing


01:06:07.547 --> 01:06:09.549
(Jonny) It's like pass the parcel.


01:06:11.801 --> 01:06:13.974
34B. Knew it.


01:06:31.321 --> 01:06:32.823
Wh at?


01:06:34.532 --> 01:06:36.284
Nothing.


01:06:47.587 --> 01:06:52.468
(Kim) Would it freak you out if I said
that was the best day of my life?


01:06:52.550 --> 01:06:57.556
OK, maybe not the best,
but certainly top... five.


01:07:00.808 --> 01:07:03.652
What is with you people
walking in on me naked?


01:07:03.728 --> 01:07:07.403
I think the idea was
you stayed below stairs, young lady.


01:07:07.482 --> 01:07:11.783
And you, don't you have
an engagement party to go to?


01:07:13.071 --> 01:07:15.449
For a second there
I thought she meant...


01:07:18.409 --> 01:07:20.286
Oh.


01:07:34.551 --> 01:07:36.849
- I did try to tell you.
- (Kim) it's not hard.


01:07:36.928 --> 01:07:39.056
"Did you hear
Jonny proposed to Chloe?"


01:07:39.138 --> 01:07:41.232
"No. Thanks for letting me know, chum."


01:07:41.307 --> 01:07:43.105
I didn't want to see you get hurt.


01:07:43.184 --> 01:07:47.530
Yeah, you just did a spiffing job
all round, didn't you?


01:07:47.605 --> 01:07:51.576
She's a chalet girl.
My God, it is such a cliché.


01:07:51.651 --> 01:07:54.154
I wouldn't have minded so much
if you were discreet


01:07:54.237 --> 01:07:57.867
but Bernhardt said you were all over
each other, on the beginner slope!


01:07:57.949 --> 01:08:01.453
Bernhardt could learn a few things
about being discreet himself.


01:08:01.536 --> 01:08:04.085
Honey, do you realise
what you're risking here?


01:08:04.163 --> 01:08:06.291
You have to stop this right now,
or I will.


01:08:06.374 --> 01:08:09.969
This isn't Jane Austen, Mum.
Look, when you and Dad met...


01:08:10.044 --> 01:08:12.138
Enough, Jonathan.


01:08:13.965 --> 01:08:15.842
I just think you can do better.


01:08:15.925 --> 01:08:18.394
Well, I don't think
Dad could have done better.


01:08:19.721 --> 01:08:22.850
Look, your father and I, we got lucky.


01:08:22.932 --> 01:08:26.061
But believe me,
this girl is only after one thing.


01:08:26.144 --> 01:08:28.146
Yeah. And it was great.


01:08:28.229 --> 01:08:31.699
- Is there a reason you're still here?
- Look, Kim, can we just...


01:08:31.774 --> 01:08:36.621
There's a noise. I can't quite...
Oh, that's right, it's a lying bastard.


01:08:36.696 --> 01:08:39.165
Yeah. OK.


01:08:39.240 --> 01:08:43.711
Erm, well, look, I owe you...
three hours.


01:08:44.912 --> 01:08:46.960
(laughs)


01:08:48.666 --> 01:08:49.713
Shit.


01:08:49.792 --> 01:08:53.296
Kim! Kim, wait! Kim!


01:08:56.174 --> 01:08:57.767
Kim!


01:09:12.523 --> 01:09:15.697
About 8:30 tomorrow.
I'll cook you a nice tea to celebrate.


01:09:15.777 --> 01:09:18.530
- What about the competition?
-I was never going to win.


01:09:18.613 --> 01:09:20.741
It's fine. I can come back
and sort you out.


01:09:20.823 --> 01:09:23.872
I've lasted three months.
I'm sure I can manage another week.


01:09:23.951 --> 01:09:27.125
Dad, I looked online
at your latest order. 24 tins of beans?


01:09:29.165 --> 01:09:31.167
Are you giving up
the chance of a lifetime


01:09:31.292 --> 01:09:33.294
because I'm eating
too many baked beans?


01:09:33.378 --> 01:09:35.472
Someone's got to take care of you.


01:09:35.546 --> 01:09:38.800
Oh, no, you don't.
Don't you dare do that, Kimmy.


01:09:38.883 --> 01:09:41.602
Don't you put this on me.
This is your decision.


01:09:41.678 --> 01:09:45.478
Anyway, since when did my Kimmy
ever say there was no way


01:09:45.556 --> 01:09:47.399
she was gonna win something?


01:09:47.475 --> 01:09:49.569
I'll tell you something else, Kimberley.


01:09:51.312 --> 01:09:52.655
What, William?


01:09:54.774 --> 01:09:57.027
It's what she would have wanted.


01:09:58.695 --> 01:10:01.039
Hallo. Was bekommst du?


01:10:02.115 --> 01:10:03.867
Erm, what do you want?


01:10:14.585 --> 01:10:17.805
It's a beautiful spring morning
here in St Anton,


01:10:17.880 --> 01:10:20.599
perfect conditions
for the open qualifiers!


01:10:21.509 --> 01:10:23.978
Come on! Come on!


01:10:29.142 --> 01:10:32.112
(commentator) _.ranks with a kicker.


01:10:32.895 --> 01:10:34.989
Mixing things up


01:10:35.064 --> 01:10:37.362
and finishing off
with a super styley 540


01:10:37.442 --> 01:10:40.787
that should see him through
to the weekend's final.


01:10:40.862 --> 01:10:45.459
And there it is, a 73!
That sends Hampton through.


01:10:45.533 --> 01:10:50.414
Next up, from Finland, Mikki Niemenan!


01:10:50.496 --> 01:10:53.796
- That's you, champ.
- Is Georgie out there?


01:10:53.875 --> 01:10:57.630
Well, don't think about her.
Think about the run. Only the run.


01:10:57.712 --> 01:10:59.885
Be the board.


01:11:03.676 --> 01:11:05.519
(start-gate monitor) Go!


01:11:06.095 --> 01:11:09.440
(commentated Here he goes,
the Finnish freak now going down,


01:11:09.515 --> 01:11:11.859
hammers those rails!


01:11:13.728 --> 01:11:16.151
Niemenan
showing some impressive skills.


01:11:17.690 --> 01:11:20.739
Switch 50-50, backside 180.


01:11:20.818 --> 01:11:24.823
Sweet! Coming up to the booter
where he fell last year.


01:11:24.906 --> 01:11:27.284
Hits it, going for broke!


01:11:27.909 --> 01:11:30.253
Whoa!


01:11:32.580 --> 01:11:34.207
And broke it is!


01:11:34.290 --> 01:11:38.466
He's up, but he's going to have
a monster headache in the morning.


01:11:39.295 --> 01:11:41.468
- You sure you want this?
- Just do it.


01:11:41.547 --> 01:11:44.676
And in the ladies' qualifiers now...


01:11:44.759 --> 01:11:46.807
Don't worry, it's legal.


01:11:50.014 --> 01:11:53.109
- Better than sex too.
- ..Tara Dakides!


01:11:54.477 --> 01:11:57.902
A solid 50-50 on the goalpost. Boom!


01:11:59.565 --> 01:12:02.489
She spread some butter on the box!


01:12:03.319 --> 01:12:06.914
And a frontside seven lean!


01:12:08.449 --> 01:12:10.793
A master class from the master!


01:12:10.868 --> 01:12:13.291
The Greek goddess!


01:12:13.371 --> 01:12:17.342
Whatever, man! She is awesome!


01:12:17.458 --> 01:12:20.132
The Queen of Scream is back!


01:12:20.211 --> 01:12:23.010
- Ow!
- Now, last up, strapped in,


01:12:23.089 --> 01:12:26.889
trying to follow an amazing run,
newcomer Kim Matthews.


01:12:26.968 --> 01:12:28.641
Let's see what she has got!


01:12:28.719 --> 01:12:32.349
Drei, zwei, eins. Go!


01:12:34.809 --> 01:12:38.188
A front 180 to switch tail, a 180 out!


01:12:38.729 --> 01:12:41.073
Textbook awesomeness!


01:12:41.148 --> 01:12:44.118
A silky tail press. Nice one, Matthews!


01:12:46.863 --> 01:12:50.242
Throwing an indy grab
coming off the box!


01:12:51.659 --> 01:12:55.289
And here she goes now,
coming up to the big booter!


01:12:55.413 --> 01:12:56.881
(car horn blares)


01:13:01.878 --> 01:13:03.425
What's happened there?


01:13:03.546 --> 01:13:06.595
She's stopped short
and takes the lame line down.


01:13:07.174 --> 01:13:11.600
Kim might have done just enough on the
top section to get into the main event.


01:13:12.930 --> 01:13:16.230
Oh, no. 59, just outside qualification.


01:13:16.309 --> 01:13:18.562
Kim will be back on finals day,


01:13:18.644 --> 01:13:21.147
but she'll have to wait and see
if she gets a ride.


01:13:21.230 --> 01:13:23.904
I came 21 st. Yay!


01:13:23.983 --> 01:13:26.111
That's great. How many qualify?


01:13:26.193 --> 01:13:30.198
The top 20. So, suddenly, not so yay.
I am first reserve though.


01:13:30.281 --> 01:13:34.127
- I get a chance if someone pulls out.
- You gave it your best shot though.


01:13:35.119 --> 01:13:36.291
(door opens)


01:13:36.370 --> 01:13:39.624
- Dad, I've got to go.
- OK, bye.


01:13:39.707 --> 01:13:41.380
Bye.


01:13:41.459 --> 01:13:43.962
- (Mikki laughs)
- Finland!


01:13:44.045 --> 01:13:46.173
Morphine rules!


01:13:46.255 --> 01:13:48.974
It's just ligaments, thank God.


01:13:53.930 --> 01:13:56.558
Oh, piss off! Again.


01:13:58.225 --> 01:13:59.693
(snoring)


01:15:12.967 --> 01:15:14.560
- (willy) Hi.
- (gasps)


01:15:19.306 --> 01:15:21.934
So you are the Yeti.


01:15:23.269 --> 01:15:24.646
Must be the hair.


01:15:59.638 --> 01:16:01.311
Want to talk about it?


01:16:06.145 --> 01:16:07.237
No.


01:16:09.857 --> 01:16:11.780
It's just something that...


01:16:23.287 --> 01:16:25.255
Er...


01:16:25.331 --> 01:16:27.174
We were...


01:16:27.249 --> 01:16:29.877
We were driving home, and, erm...


01:16:29.960 --> 01:16:31.587
I'd just won the London Trials


01:16:31.670 --> 01:16:34.469
and... all of us in the car,


01:16:34.548 --> 01:16:36.050
me and my mum and dad,


01:16:36.133 --> 01:16:38.386
were singing at the top of our voices


01:16:38.469 --> 01:16:41.894
and we were all laughing
cos none of us can sing for shit.


01:16:41.972 --> 01:16:44.020
And, erm...


01:16:45.476 --> 01:16:47.353
Er...


01:16:47.436 --> 01:16:49.939
My dad had to swerve, and...


01:16:51.816 --> 01:16:54.114
And he skidded off the road.


01:16:57.488 --> 01:16:59.035
And my...


01:17:01.826 --> 01:17:04.670
My mum was on the side
that got hit, and...


01:17:08.749 --> 01:17:10.922
And she died.


01:17:12.920 --> 01:17:14.968
My mum died.


01:17:19.426 --> 01:17:21.349
I just really miss her.


01:17:33.858 --> 01:17:35.826
Sorry. I'm so sorry.


01:17:37.611 --> 01:17:40.239
I always get like this
when I'm around Yetis.


01:17:46.871 --> 01:17:48.544
Let's ride.


01:17:51.500 --> 01:17:56.802
(Willy) I always tell the mountains
my problems. They're good listeners.


01:18:44.303 --> 01:18:47.853
Two minutes. I'm going to go
and tell the caterers.


01:18:54.313 --> 01:18:55.815
(man) Jonathan!


01:18:55.940 --> 01:18:58.193
Deidre and I would like to say...


01:18:58.275 --> 01:19:00.903
Lord and Lady Marberry,
can I get you another drink?


01:19:00.986 --> 01:19:04.115
Well, why not? Good to see you.


01:19:05.574 --> 01:19:07.542
If you've got to do it, do it now.


01:19:12.748 --> 01:19:18.005
He had it the entire time we were there
and I had no idea. Such a surprise.


01:19:18.087 --> 01:19:21.011
- Excuse me. Can I have a word?
- Yeah.


01:19:21.090 --> 01:19:22.967
Thanks.


01:19:23.050 --> 01:19:24.723
What's up?


01:19:26.679 --> 01:19:28.272
Wh at?


01:19:30.182 --> 01:19:32.401
- What is it?
- Erm...


01:19:32.476 --> 01:19:35.446
I have an idea
that I wanted to run by you.


01:19:38.357 --> 01:19:42.703
How-How would you feel
if we didn't get married?


01:19:42.778 --> 01:19:44.780
How would that sit with you?


01:19:47.783 --> 01:19:53.381
- Good idea.
- Really? You're OK with this?


01:19:54.748 --> 01:19:56.796
Of course I'm not OK with it.


01:19:58.544 --> 01:20:01.593
- Look, I understand it's bad timing.
- Do you really?


01:20:01.672 --> 01:20:05.677
Ending a five-year relationship
in the middle of our engagement party?


01:20:05.759 --> 01:20:08.979
Yes, I think that constitutes
bad timing!


01:20:09.054 --> 01:20:10.977
(room falls silent)


01:20:11.056 --> 01:20:14.981
- I'm sorry, I'm...
- An asshole is what you are!


01:20:18.689 --> 01:20:20.942
Exactly right. I am.


01:20:24.528 --> 01:20:26.951
You're in love with her, aren't you?


01:20:31.535 --> 01:20:34.664
Exactly right. I am.


01:20:45.007 --> 01:20:47.726
Someday I will probably
thank you for this,


01:20:47.801 --> 01:20:51.476
for not going through with it
just to please your mother.


01:20:53.724 --> 01:20:55.647
But today...


01:20:57.269 --> 01:20:59.192
(all gasp)


01:21:03.567 --> 01:21:06.912
Today, it's not quite how I'm feeling.


01:21:08.364 --> 01:21:11.709
Here, I got you some ice
for the swelling.


01:21:14.161 --> 01:21:16.209
They're gonna blow up.


01:21:20.000 --> 01:21:22.173
Come on, let's go.


01:21:23.921 --> 01:21:26.299
- And for your next trick...
- You're not upset?


01:21:26.382 --> 01:21:28.805
She's lovely, but I trust you.


01:21:28.884 --> 01:21:31.933
- Your mother, on the other hand...
- (wine glass tings)


01:21:34.348 --> 01:21:37.978
Ladies and gentlemen,
I give you the happy couple.


01:21:38.060 --> 01:21:40.404
In the unlikely event
of an emergency landing,


01:21:40.479 --> 01:21:43.824
the cabin crew will direct you
to the nearest available exit.


01:21:43.899 --> 01:21:45.901
It was like love at first sight.


01:21:45.984 --> 01:21:48.783
They were kids,
if you can believe that.


01:21:49.571 --> 01:21:54.418
(sighs) OK, baby. Let's get you drunk.


01:21:55.869 --> 01:21:59.749
Oh, my God. Oh, my God!


01:21:59.832 --> 01:22:01.254
Yeah, laters, babe. Yeah.


01:22:01.333 --> 01:22:03.961
Oh, my God!
You guys are never going to believe


01:22:04.044 --> 01:22:05.717
what happened to Jonny and Chloe.


01:22:05.796 --> 01:22:09.801
Apparently there was this major
showdown at their engagement party.


01:22:09.883 --> 01:22:12.557
Hattie says Chloe dumped Jonny
in front of everyone


01:22:12.636 --> 01:22:14.388
and Jonny stormed out.


01:22:14.471 --> 01:22:17.600
But Pips also tweeted that it was
Jonny who broke up with Chloe


01:22:17.683 --> 01:22:20.061
and Chloe just passed out, right there.


01:22:20.144 --> 01:22:23.114
Either way,
it was just super-dramatic, right?


01:22:29.736 --> 01:22:31.488
Wh at?


01:22:31.572 --> 01:22:33.666
I couldn't care less.


01:22:37.661 --> 01:22:43.088
Welcome to Channel 419, broadcasting
live from St Anton, Austria.


01:22:43.167 --> 01:22:45.795
Let's go to our girl on the scene,
Jasmine Kendal.


01:22:45.878 --> 01:22:49.382
So it's finals day here in St Anton,
and one shot is all they get.


01:22:49.465 --> 01:22:51.513
Come on, y'all. Let's make some noise!


01:22:52.843 --> 01:22:56.564
The Roxy Slopestyle Pro! Whoo!


01:22:56.638 --> 01:23:01.439
Come on, let this be the best event in
the history of snowboarding! Let's go!


01:23:01.518 --> 01:23:03.771
Whoo!


01:23:03.854 --> 01:23:06.482
(man) Good luck, Kim.
I hope you get a ride.


01:23:06.565 --> 01:23:09.739
(Kim) Yeah, well, fingers crossed.


01:23:09.818 --> 01:23:11.695
Thanks, Gunter.


01:23:14.072 --> 01:23:16.120
Whoa, whoa, this area is reserved.


01:23:16.200 --> 01:23:18.373
- Well, I'm the reserve.
- Oh, yes?


01:23:18.452 --> 01:23:21.046
- Your tick here?
- Does it really matter?


01:23:21.121 --> 01:23:24.716
- (Willy) You're not listening.
- (Tara) Enough. I'm doing it already.


01:23:26.793 --> 01:23:28.591
Thanks.


01:23:28.670 --> 01:23:32.345
(commentator)
20th qualifier, Anja Schmidt!


01:23:32.424 --> 01:23:35.268
By my count, nice. That's an 84!


01:23:36.386 --> 01:23:39.310
Bethany Loux, getting high!
She's looking good!


01:23:40.432 --> 01:23:43.026
Uh-oh, that bump's gonna cost her.


01:23:43.727 --> 01:23:48.358
Halfway through the competition now,
and this thing is still wide open.


01:23:48.440 --> 01:23:51.319
What's this? A front flip! Yes!


01:23:51.401 --> 01:23:54.200
Awesome-tacularl


01:23:58.700 --> 01:24:01.670
Some major amplitude on that hit! Sick!


01:24:02.788 --> 01:24:06.292
Deep in the final stages.
It is getting tense!


01:24:07.834 --> 01:24:10.838
Oh. And a super-smooth 720.


01:24:10.921 --> 01:24:14.141
That takes Kjersti Buaas
into top spot!


01:24:16.718 --> 01:24:19.392
Final three competitors
to the gate, please.


01:24:19.471 --> 01:24:24.773
Howson, Beal and... Dakides.


01:24:24.851 --> 01:24:28.446
You see, you must have a system
or else everything fails.


01:24:28.522 --> 01:24:31.366
Now, my friend, my work here is done.


01:24:33.151 --> 01:24:35.654
- Hey.
- Just wanted to say good luck.


01:24:35.737 --> 01:24:37.239
Thanks.


01:24:38.740 --> 01:24:41.209
Hey, you killed it in qualifying,
you know that?


01:24:41.285 --> 01:24:45.335
- Up to the point where I screwed up.
- Yeah. Up until then.


01:24:45.414 --> 01:24:47.337
(Willy) OK, Tara, it's ready.


01:24:49.001 --> 01:24:51.254
- Well, I'll leave you to it.
- Thanks.


01:24:53.589 --> 01:24:57.560
Pretty near perfect yesterday, babe.
What's left to prove?


01:25:11.106 --> 01:25:14.201
Hey, Kim. Come back.


01:25:19.615 --> 01:25:22.539
- You're riding.
- But no one's dropped out.


01:25:32.085 --> 01:25:35.555
Try not to screw up this time, huh?


01:25:35.631 --> 01:25:40.808
Hey, clipboard guy. I'm pulling out.
I gave my bib to Kim.


01:25:47.309 --> 01:25:50.939
- Last up, lead qualifier...
- Hold on.


01:25:51.021 --> 01:25:56.949
Wait... I'm being told that
Tara Dakides has had to pull out.


01:25:57.027 --> 01:26:01.248
Her place is being taken
by Kim Matthews from the UK.


01:26:01.323 --> 01:26:02.870
(yells)


01:26:06.286 --> 01:26:08.539
(phone rings)


01:26:13.001 --> 01:26:14.844
- Hello?
- (Kim) Channel 419.


01:26:14.920 --> 01:26:17.218
I'm on. Now.


01:26:26.390 --> 01:26:28.142
Ready?


01:26:33.980 --> 01:26:37.610
J' Oh, take these storms away,
start a brand-new story


01:26:37.693 --> 01:26:41.197
J' I'll make it through each day,
singing death or glory


01:26:41.321 --> 01:26:43.369
- I Lord won't answer me
- Drei...


01:26:43.448 --> 01:26:46.577
- J' I won't let it bring me down
- Zwei, eins...


01:26:46.660 --> 01:26:47.752
Go!


01:26:49.996 --> 01:26:52.340
What channel? Now?


01:26:52.416 --> 01:26:54.259
Cheers, Bill. Les!


01:26:57.963 --> 01:27:00.466
(commentator)
Kim 's coming up to the table.


01:27:04.094 --> 01:27:05.220
- Come on.
- I Hold on


01:27:06.555 --> 01:27:08.398
I Hold on


01:27:09.224 --> 01:27:14.230
On the goalpost,
backside boardslide. Nice!


01:27:20.444 --> 01:27:21.445
Yes!


01:27:21.528 --> 01:27:24.828
Now what has she saved up for last?


01:27:40.672 --> 01:27:43.892
J* Hold on, hold on


01:27:43.967 --> 01:27:47.392
I Where we belong


01:27:47.471 --> 01:27:52.398
J* My heart, my song


01:27:52.476 --> 01:27:55.320
J* We stand alone


01:27:55.395 --> 01:28:00.026
I Where we belong


01:28:00.108 --> 01:28:03.032
(commentator) Switch rodeo 900!


01:28:03.111 --> 01:28:05.614
She is so sweet, my teeth hurt!


01:28:08.283 --> 01:28:09.455
Yes!


01:28:17.417 --> 01:28:19.761
Hey, whoa! Let's stay professional!


01:28:19.836 --> 01:28:22.840
I'm her agent. All offers to me!


01:28:24.800 --> 01:28:26.973
Ow. Ooh. Ow.


01:28:27.052 --> 01:28:29.054
You were amazing, Betty.


01:28:29.638 --> 01:28:31.811
Pull your chequebooks and follow me.


01:28:31.890 --> 01:28:34.689
(Georgie) She's my friend!
I saw her first!


01:28:34.768 --> 01:28:37.521
(all shriek)


01:28:40.023 --> 01:28:41.866
(Jonny) Congratulations.


01:28:41.942 --> 01:28:45.992
So I guess your hourly rate
just shot through the roof.


01:28:46.071 --> 01:28:49.871
Oh, right. It's the lying bastard.


01:28:49.950 --> 01:28:55.081
- Technically, I never lied to you.
- Withholding-the-truth bastard.


01:28:56.915 --> 01:28:59.259
You hurt me, you know.


01:29:02.546 --> 01:29:03.889
Look...


01:29:05.006 --> 01:29:09.386
I'm sorry. I really am.
You know it's over...


01:29:09.469 --> 01:29:13.144
Things are gonna have to change
now I'm a global snowboarding megastar.


01:29:16.518 --> 01:29:19.772
You're right. You're completely
out of my league.


01:29:19.855 --> 01:29:21.482
(Kim) Hm-hmm.


01:29:21.565 --> 01:29:25.786
It would be really awkward
if I was always paying for everything.


01:29:25.861 --> 01:29:27.989
I could be a kept man.


01:29:29.781 --> 01:29:31.499
(Kim) Come here!


01:29:34.828 --> 01:29:37.456
I've never kissed a girl
in a helmet before.


01:29:37.539 --> 01:29:39.257
Safety first.


01:29:48.300 --> 01:29:49.768
(Jonny) Oh, God.


01:29:49.843 --> 01:29:52.312
We don't have a license for that stuff!


01:30:00.020 --> 01:30:01.237
Alright.


01:30:01.313 --> 01:30:03.315
Kim, come up here and get your prize!


01:30:08.528 --> 01:30:10.246
That was so beautiful.


01:30:12.490 --> 01:30:16.370
Georgie, from the moment
I laid eyes on you,


01:30:16.494 --> 01:30:18.667
I knew that one day
we would be together


01:30:18.747 --> 01:30:21.091
and now seeing you here I...


01:30:23.001 --> 01:30:25.220
Shitballs.


01:30:26.379 --> 01:30:29.599
How about you?
Want to catch a gondola?


01:30:29.674 --> 01:30:31.551
- OK.
- Really?


01:30:34.220 --> 01:30:38.976
And in first place, winning $25,000,


01:30:39.059 --> 01:30:43.656
please welcome to the podium
Kim Matthews!


01:30:43.730 --> 01:30:45.403
(crowd roars)


01:30:55.200 --> 01:30:59.922
(commentated What a future
this girl has ahead of her! Amazing!


01:31:28.775 --> 01:31:31.278
.P You say everything 's alright


01:31:31.361 --> 01:31:35.241
.P I say nothing can go right, yeah


01:31:35.323 --> 01:31:37.200
J' Oh, what a game you can play


01:31:39.327 --> 01:31:41.955
J' Sad days add to confusion


01:31:42.038 --> 01:31:45.918
J' Sad ways end in delusion, yeah


01:31:46.001 --> 01:31:47.674
.P That's the name of the game


01:31:49.295 --> 01:31:51.844
.P Well, I know your love is rough


01:31:51.923 --> 01:31:54.722
I And the road you take is tough


01:31:54.801 --> 01:31:57.054
I But I just can't get enough


01:31:57.137 --> 01:31:58.639
I Chequered love


01:31:58.722 --> 01:32:02.647
- Erm...
- I'm trying a bit of the old gourmet.


01:32:02.726 --> 01:32:05.400
(laughs)
Oh, yeah? Who's the lucky lady?


01:32:05.478 --> 01:32:06.821
You are?


01:32:09.315 --> 01:32:11.158
I mean, only if you want to.


01:32:11.234 --> 01:32:12.861
I mean, I only said that


01:32:12.944 --> 01:32:14.867
cos I thought it sounded cool.


01:32:14.946 --> 01:32:19.326
- I finish work at six.
- Six is good.


01:32:19.409 --> 01:32:21.958
See you at six, then.


01:32:23.830 --> 01:32:26.174
.P Well, I know your love is rough


01:32:26.249 --> 01:32:28.843
I And the road you take is tough


01:32:28.918 --> 01:32:31.137
I But I just can't get enough


01:32:31.212 --> 01:32:33.214
I Chequered love


01:32:33.298 --> 01:32:35.551
(presented Kim, this is big.


01:32:35.675 --> 01:32:39.725
You know, pro snowboarder,
sponsorship deals all over the place.


01:32:39.804 --> 01:32:42.557
And you totally rocked up
with some hot guy.


01:32:42.640 --> 01:32:46.816
- So that's brilliant.
- He just keeps following me around.


01:32:46.895 --> 01:32:50.399
If you want me to take him off your
hands, that is something I could do.


01:32:50.482 --> 01:32:53.361
Yeah. We could sort of share him.


01:32:55.070 --> 01:32:56.196
I Chequered love


01:33:01.242 --> 01:33:03.916
.P You say everything 's alright


01:33:03.995 --> 01:33:07.795
.P I say nothing can go right, yeah


01:33:07.874 --> 01:33:09.251
J' Oh, what a game you can play


01:33:09.334 --> 01:33:12.213
- (Jules) Oh! Nigel!
- (Nigel groans)


01:33:12.295 --> 01:33:14.844
(Nigel) Jules, we did it!
It's under 90 seconds!


01:33:14.923 --> 01:33:16.425
(Jules) Well done, babes.


01:33:16.508 --> 01:33:20.638
J' Oh, I can't let go


01:33:20.762 --> 01:33:22.435
.P Cos I need you so tonight


01:33:40.240 --> 01:33:44.086
Whoo-hoo!


01:33:44.160 --> 01:33:45.412
- Oh _
- (laughter)


01:33:45.495 --> 01:33:47.497
I Chequered love


01:33:49.624 --> 01:33:51.376
(man) Action.


01:33:51.459 --> 01:33:53.632
- This is your fault.
- You are welcome.


01:33:53.711 --> 01:33:54.712
(glass smashes)


01:33:54.838 --> 01:33:57.387
- Oh.
- (beep)
